# Thread-Safe LRU + TTL Cache in Rust

## Design Overview

The core tension is that LRU bookkeeping requires mutating state on every read (to update recency), so a single global lock becomes a bottleneck under load, and `RwLock` doesn't help because `get` is effectively a write operation.

The standard high-performance approach (used by `dashmap`, Caffeine, etc.) is **sharding**: split the keyspace into N independent shards, each with its own lock. Threads hashing to different shards never contend.

Key choices:
- **Sharded `parking_lot::Mutex`** for low overhead and fairness.
- **Slab arena + indices** for the LRU doubly-linked list (avoids `Rc`/`RefCell` and stays `Send + Sync`).
- **Lazy expiration** on `get` plus an optional **background janitor** thread for proactive cleanup.
- **`ahash`** for fast, DoS-resistant key hashing into shards.

```
Cache
 ├─ shards: [Mutex<Shard>; N]   ← N is power of two
 └─ hasher: RandomState

Shard
 ├─ map:    HashMap<K, usize>   ← key -> slab index
 ├─ nodes:  Slab<Node<K,V>>     ← arena of LRU nodes
 ├─ head:   Option<usize>       ← MRU
 ├─ tail:   Option<usize>       ← LRU (eviction target)
 └─ capacity: usize             ← per-shard

Node { key, value, expires_at, prev, next }
```

## Cargo Dependencies

```toml
[dependencies]
parking_lot = "0.12"
slab        = "0.4"
ahash       = "0.8"
```

## Implementation

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::hash::{BuildHasher, Hash, Hasher};
use std::sync::Arc;
use std::time::{Duration, Instant};

use parking_lot::Mutex;
use slab::Slab;

const DEFAULT_SHARDS: usize = 16;

struct Node<K, V> {
    key: K,
    value: V,
    expires_at: Option<Instant>,
    prev: Option<usize>,
    next: Option<usize>,
}

struct Shard<K, V> {
    map: HashMap<K, usize>,
    nodes: Slab<Node<K, V>>,
    head: Option<usize>, // MRU
    tail: Option<usize>, // LRU
    capacity: usize,
}

impl<K: Eq + Hash + Clone, V> Shard<K, V> {
    fn new(capacity: usize) -> Self {
        Self {
            map: HashMap::with_capacity(capacity),
            nodes: Slab::with_capacity(capacity),
            head: None,
            tail: None,
            capacity: capacity.max(1),
        }
    }

    fn detach(&mut self, idx: usize) {
        let (prev, next) = {
            let n = &self.nodes[idx];
            (n.prev, n.next)
        };
        match prev {
            Some(p) => self.nodes[p].next = next,
            None => self.head = next,
        }
        match next {
            Some(n) => self.nodes[n].prev = prev,
            None => self.tail = prev,
        }
        let n = &mut self.nodes[idx];
        n.prev = None;
        n.next = None;
    }

    fn attach_front(&mut self, idx: usize) {
        let old_head = self.head;
        let n = &mut self.nodes[idx];
        n.prev = None;
        n.next = old_head;
        match old_head {
            Some(h) => self.nodes[h].prev = Some(idx),
            None => self.tail = Some(idx), // list was empty
        }
        self.head = Some(idx);
    }

    fn touch(&mut self, idx: usize) {
        if self.head == Some(idx) {
            return;
        }
        self.detach(idx);
        self.attach_front(idx);
    }

    fn get(&mut self, key: &K, now: Instant) -> Option<V>
    where
        V: Clone,
    {
        let idx = *self.map.get(key)?;
        if let Some(exp) = self.nodes[idx].expires_at {
            if now >= exp {
                self.remove_idx(idx);
                return None;
            }
        }
        self.touch(idx);
        Some(self.nodes[idx].value.clone())
    }

    fn insert(
        &mut self,
        key: K,
        value: V,
        ttl: Option<Duration>,
        now: Instant,
    ) -> Option<V> {
        let expires_at = ttl.map(|d| now + d);
        if let Some(&idx) = self.map.get(&key) {
            let old = std::mem::replace(&mut self.nodes[idx].value, value);
            self.nodes[idx].expires_at = expires_at;
            self.touch(idx);
            return Some(old);
        }
        if self.map.len() >= self.capacity {
            self.evict_lru();
        }
        let idx = self.nodes.insert(Node {
            key: key.clone(),
            value,
            expires_at,
            prev: None,
            next: None,
        });
        self.attach_front(idx);
        self.map.insert(key, idx);
        None
    }

    fn remove_idx(&mut self, idx: usize) -> Option<V> {
        self.detach(idx);
        let node = self.nodes.remove(idx);
        self.map.remove(&node.key);
        Some(node.value)
    }

    fn remove(&mut self, key: &K) -> Option<V> {
        let idx = self.map.remove(key)?;
        self.detach(idx);
        Some(self.nodes.remove(idx).value)
    }

    fn evict_lru(&mut self) -> Option<(K, V)> {
        let tail = self.tail?;
        self.detach(tail);
        let node = self.nodes.remove(tail);
        self.map.remove(&node.key);
        Some((node.key, node.value))
    }

    fn purge_expired(&mut self, now: Instant) {
        let stale: Vec<usize> = self
            .nodes
            .iter()
            .filter_map(|(i, n)| match n.expires_at {
                Some(exp) if now >= exp => Some(i),
                _ => None,
            })
            .collect();
        for idx in stale {
            self.detach(idx);
            let node = self.nodes.remove(idx);
            self.map.remove(&node.key);
        }
    }

    fn len(&self) -> usize {
        self.map.len()
    }
}

pub struct Cache<K, V> {
    shards: Box<[Mutex<Shard<K, V>>]>,
    hasher: ahash::RandomState,
    default_ttl: Option<Duration>,
}

impl<K, V> Cache<K, V>
where
    K: Eq + Hash + Clone + Send + Sync + 'static,
    V: Clone + Send + Sync + 'static,
{
    pub fn new(capacity: usize, default_ttl: Option<Duration>) -> Arc<Self> {
        Self::with_shards(capacity, DEFAULT_SHARDS, default_ttl)
    }

    pub fn with_shards(
        capacity: usize,
        num_shards: usize,
        default_ttl: Option<Duration>,
    ) -> Arc<Self> {
        let num_shards = num_shards.next_power_of_two().max(1);
        let per_shard = (capacity + num_shards - 1) / num_shards;
        let shards = (0..num_shards)
            .map(|_| Mutex::new(Shard::new(per_shard)))
            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
            .into_boxed_slice();
        Arc::new(Self {
            shards,
            hasher: ahash::RandomState::new(),
            default_ttl,
        })
    }

    #[inline]
    fn shard_idx(&self, key: &K) -> usize {
        let mut h = self.hasher.build_hasher();
        key.hash(&mut h);
        (h.finish() as usize) & (self.shards.len() - 1)
    }

    pub fn get(&self, key: &K) -> Option<V> {
        let i = self.shard_idx(key);
        self.shards[i].lock().get(key, Instant::now())
    }

    pub fn insert(&self, key: K, value: V) -> Option<V> {
        self.insert_inner(key, value, self.default_ttl)
    }

    pub fn insert_with_ttl(&self, key: K, value: V, ttl: Duration) -> Option<V> {
        self.insert_inner(key, value, Some(ttl))
    }

    fn insert_inner(&self, key: K, value: V, ttl: Option<Duration>) -> Option<V> {
        let i = self.shard_idx(&key);
        self.shards[i].lock().insert(key, value, ttl, Instant::now())
    }

    pub fn remove(&self, key: &K) -> Option<V> {
        let i = self.shard_idx(key);
        self.shards[i].lock().remove(key)
    }

    pub fn len(&self) -> usize {
        self.shards.iter().map(|s| s.lock().len()).sum()
    }

    pub fn purge_expired(&self) {
        let now = Instant::now();
        for s in self.shards.iter() {
            s.lock().purge_expired(now);
        }
    }

    /// Spawns a background janitor. Holds only a `Weak` ref so the cache
    /// can still be dropped; the thread exits when no strong refs remain.
    pub fn start_janitor(self: &Arc<Self>, interval: Duration) {
        let weak = Arc::downgrade(self);
        std::thread::spawn(move || loop {
            std::thread::sleep(interval);
            match weak.upgrade() {
                Some(cache) => cache.purge_expired(),
                None => break,
            }
        });
    }
}
```

## Usage

```rust
use std::time::Duration;

let cache = Cache::<String, Vec<u8>>::new(10_000, Some(Duration::from_secs(60)));
cache.start_janitor(Duration::from_secs(5));

cache.insert("user:42".to_string(), b"payload".to_vec());
cache.insert_with_ttl("session:abc".to_string(), vec![1, 2, 3], Duration::from_secs(10));

if let Some(v) = cache.get(&"user:42".to_string()) {
    println!("hit: {} bytes", v.len());
}

// Cheap to share across threads:
let c2 = cache.clone();
std::thread::spawn(move || {
    c2.insert("from-thread".into(), vec![]);
});
```

## Why This Design Performs Well

- **Sharding** scales linearly with shard count for uncorrelated keys. With 16 shards, contention probability drops ~16x versus a single lock.
- **`parking_lot::Mutex`** is ~1 word, has fast uncontended paths, and parks rather than spinning on contention.
- **Slab + indices** gives O(1) allocation and free for LRU nodes without per-node heap allocation, and sidesteps Rust's pain with self-referential linked lists.
- **Lazy TTL** keeps the read path cheap: just one `Instant` comparison if the entry has a TTL.
- **`ahash`** is significantly faster than `SipHash` (the default) and still keyed against HashDoS.

## Trade-offs and Extensions Worth Knowing

- **Reads take a write lock.** That's fundamental to strict LRU. If reads dominate and you can tolerate approximate recency, switch to a **CLOCK** or **W-TinyLFU** policy: record reads in a thread-local ring buffer and drain it under a lock occasionally (this is Caffeine's secret). Massive throughput win.
- **Capacity by entry count, not bytes.** For byte-bounded caches, add a `weight: usize` per entry and evict until under the byte limit.
- **`V: Clone` on `get`.** For large values, return `Arc<V>` instead so cloning is a refcount bump.
- **TTL purge is O(n).** Fine for periodic janitors; for very large caches, add a min-heap of `(expires_at, idx)` per shard for O(log n) expiration.
- **No async API.** The locks are short-held, so calling from async is generally fine, but for very contended workloads expose a `tokio::task::spawn_blocking` wrapper or use `tokio::sync::Mutex`.
- **No metrics.** Add `AtomicU64` counters per shard for hits/misses/evictions if you need observability.
